cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this archive, please cite it as below."
title: "Riemann: an AI-orchestrated research archive of approaches to the Riemann Hypothesis"
abstract: >-
  A curated, annotated archive of every major serious approach to the Riemann
  Hypothesis (178 primary sources across six approach families, six annotated
  bibliographies, and a synthesis), together with a numerical and computer-assisted
  (Arb ball-arithmetic) laboratory studying Weil positivity in the critical support
  window. The archive proves no new mathematics about RH; its original contributions
  are a few elementary lemmas, rigorous subspace certificates with active prime terms,
  an exact reformulation of the one-prime positivity target, and an honest map of the
  barriers and openings. Built by AI research agents under human direction.
type: dataset
authors:
